<title>ITALY: DeBenedetti's CIR shares fall in Milan.</title>
<headline>DeBenedetti's CIR shares fall in Milan.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in De Benedetti family holding CIR, which had climbed nine percent on the bourse earlier, turned negative to stand 0.59 percent down at 710 lire by 0945 GMT.</p>
<p>CIR raced higher on a French newspaper report that French company CGIP was expected to launch a bid for Cerus this week but fell when CGIP said it had no plans to launch a public offer for the company or car parts maker Valeo.</p>
<p>CIR controls Cerus, which is De Benedetti's French holding company. Cerus in turn controls 28 percent of Valeo.</p>
</text>
